      SUBROUTINE GETDETECT(ODFILE,ISTAT)
C     =================================
C
C---- Given an image filename, identifies  detector type from
C     header information, and reads header info.
C
C     Currently will recognise Mar300, Mar345, MarCCD, ADSC, Raxis2,
C     Raxis4, Raxis 5 detectors, Jupiter, Saturn, Bruker Smart, DIP2000
C     series (not tested for 25 or 40cm plates...)
C
C     ***** IMPORTANT *****
C     Note that if this is an HDF5 file, then it is assumed to be an Eiger
C     detector. While only Eigers write HDF5 at present, this situation
C     may change in the future. Also, there is no way to distinguish Eiger
C     and Eiger2 detectors (which have modules of different sizes). Currently
C     this is done based on the size of the image and in any case it only affects
C     the way that the tile gaps are set up (in GETGAPS).
C
C     ODFILE      Full filename of image including directory if not current dir
C
C     ISTAT       Status flag (returned)
C                 0   No errors
C                 1   Detector not recognised
C              -999   File does not exist
C                -1   Error in reading image header
C                -2   Cannot find terminator "}" in header
C                -3   Error in reading remainder of header (beyond 512 bytes)
C
      IMPLICIT NONE
C
C
C     .. Parameters ..
C&&*&& include  ../inc/parameter.f
C
C $Id: parameter.f,v 1.34 2020/12/15 20:08:54 andrew Exp $
C
C--- awk generated include file  parameter.h
C---- START of include file parameter.h
C
